# Third-party notices: Rust dependencies

AXIS CAM Studio is MIT licensed. The Rust crates it is built from keep the licenses of their authors; this file lists each of them with the full text of the licenses that apply. It is generated by `scripts/generate-notices.sh` from `Cargo.lock` and covers the normal dependencies of the macOS, Windows and Linux builds (not build-only or test-only crates). Components that are not Rust crates (Open CASCADE and its libraries, Clipper2, Fidget's source notice, the UC100 driver) are described in `THIRD_PARTY.md`.

## MPL-2.0 crates

fidget, fidget-core and fidget-mesh (0.4.3) and option-ext (0.2.0, used by `dirs`) are under MPL-2.0. They are used unmodified. Their source is available at <https://github.com/mkeeter/fidget/tree/v0.4.3> and <https://github.com/soc/option-ext>, or from the crates.io archives for the versions locked in `Cargo.lock`. The MPL-2.0 text is below and in `fidget-MPL-2.0.txt`.

